  "body": "Legacy course registration selected accounts by shared contact details and could create credentials or student access. This change creates an unverified enquiry contact inside an atomic, source-scoped request transaction, without account adoption or access grants.\n\nFallback enquiries and payable checkout now share a receipt and lock. Retries preserve the accepted registration and checkout details across feature-flag or policy changes; overlapping submissions converge without duplicate contacts, follow-ups or payment effects. Separate attendees can share an email. Changed accepted input conflicts, and unsupported request-key punctuation returns 400 before writes. WhatsApp operations have a separate server-controlled namespace. Administrative lazy links lock and re-read the registration.\n\nDepends on merged #434. Append-only migration 110 preserves its exercised introduction and refuses destructive rollback after receipts exist. Web forms retain retry keys after uncertain failures and edits.\n\nValidation: 10 dedicated PostgreSQL cases passed, including concurrency across checkout enablement, both flag transitions, shared-email attendees, transactional failure, actor/source isolation and zero payment attempts. Full backend: 2,585 examples, zero failures, four separately exercised PostgreSQL suites pending in that general run. Four web form tests, TypeScript, focused lint and catalog audit passed. Staging migration replay, backup restoration and private ACL verification passed. Application staging verification and production deployment remain pending. See docs/identity/course-prevention.md.\n",
